                <pb facs="0142" n="132" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg132"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M) Portugal/1537: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Norweb</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-09T19:00:00-04:00">June 9, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1680. Reference your 1755, June 7, and London’s 4569, June 7. Department and FEA
                    entirely agree with proposal to cancel surcharges. Sent to Lisbon, repeated to
                    London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
